// EXPECT_STDOUT 42
//
// 221.1 №979. A sum variant and a free function share the name `Red`.
//
// The checker resolves the CALL `Red()` to the function and types it `int`
// (it records the callee in `resolved_callees`, types/mod.rs:17570). Codegen
// used to ignore that and substitute the variant constructor, emitting
// `nova_print_int(nova_make_Color_Red())` — so the C compiler refused a program
// the checker had passed. Fixed by asking the checker's answer before falling
// back to the name-based variant heuristic.
//
// The spec is SILENT on whether a variant name may be shadowed this way
// (searched 2026-09-06: prohibition wording, property wording, and D-block
// headings about sums — nothing). So this fixture pins the CHECKER's rule, and
// the point it really pins is narrower and firmer: codegen must not contradict
// the checker. If the language later reserves variant names, the refusal
// belongs in the checker and this fixture becomes a negative — but codegen
// following the checker stays right either way.
module standalone.p979_fn_shadows_variant_name

type Color enum Red | Green

fn Red() -> int => 42

fn main() Io -> () => println(Red())
